Probably not the right thread  but it's just occured to me that we need 
another field in jbovlaste for lujvo subclasses e.g. jvajvo/ non-jvajvo....

Then it'd be much easier to understand which lujvo place structure we have 
to remember (like zi'evla) and which lujvo are made by a transparent 
algorithm and are in fact compressed bridi.

